{"name":"Almond Roca","hex":"#f0e8e0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"almond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The seed within the drupe of a small deciduous tree in family Rosaceae, Prunus amygdalus, considered a culinary nut.","The tree that produces almonds."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Brownish, resembling the colour of an almond nut."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/almond"}],"entries":[{"title":"Almond Roca","blocks":[{"text":"Almond Roca is a brand of chocolate-covered, hard toffee with a coating of ground almonds. It is similar to chocolate-covered English toffee. The candy is manufactured by the Brown & Haley Co. of Tacoma, Washington, founded in 1912 by Harry Brown and J.C. Haley."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Almond_Roca.JPG/330px-Almond_Roca.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almond_Roca","wikidata":"Q4733892"},{"title":"Almond","blocks":[{"text":"The almond is a species of tree from the genus Prunus. Along with the peach, it is classified in the subgenus Amygdalus, distinguished from the other subgenera by corrugations on the woody shell (endocarp) surrounding the seed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg/330px-Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almond","wikidata":"Q15545507"},{"title":"List of Crayola crayon colors","blocks":[{"text":"Since the introduction of Crayola drawing crayons by Binney & Smith in 1903, more than 200 colors have been produced in a wide variety of assortments. The table below represents all of the colors found in regular Crayola assortments from 1903 to the present. Since the introduction of fluorescent crayons in the 1970s, the standard colors have been complemented by a number of specialty crayon assortments, represented in subsequent tables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Crayola1.jpg/330px-Crayola1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Crayola_crayon_colors","wikidata":"Q6568034"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/108-112_EAST_26TH_ST._STILLSON-KELLOGG_SHOE_FACTORY%2C_NOW_BROWN-HALEY_CANDY_FACTORY_%281902%29._-_Union_Depot_Area_Study%2C_Tacoma%2C_Pierce_County%2C_WA_HABS_WASH%2C27-TACO%2C6-41.tif/lossy-page1-500px-thumbnail.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/108-112_EAST_26TH_ST._STILLSON-KELLOGG_SHOE_FACTORY%2C_NOW_BROWN-HALEY_CANDY_FACTORY_%281902%29._-_Union_Depot_Area_Study%2C_Tacoma%2C_Pierce_County%2C_WA_HABS_WASH%2C27-TACO%2C6-41.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-thumbnail.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/108-112_EAST_26TH_ST._STILLSON-KELLOGG_SHOE_FACTORY%2C_NOW_BROWN-HALEY_CANDY_FACTORY_%281902%29._-_Union_Depot_Area_Study%2C_Tacoma%2C_Pierce_County%2C_WA_HABS_WASH%2C27-TACO%2C6-41.tif/lossy-page1-500px-thumbnail.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Brown & Haley factory, Tacoma","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A108-112_EAST_26TH_ST._STILLSON-KELLOGG_SHOE_FACTORY%2C_NOW_BROWN-HALEY_CANDY_FACTORY_(1902)._-_Union_Depot_Area_Study%2C_Tacoma%2C_Pierce_County%2C_WA_HABS_WASH%2C27-TACO%2C6-41.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Ametllesjuliol.jpg/500px-Ametllesjuliol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Ametllesjulio